   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "um … zu: in order to",
     "texto": [
      "**Um** + infinitive with **zu** expresses purpose and is usually used when the subject is the same: **Ich fahre mit dem Zug, um Geld zu sparen** (I go by train to save money). The infinitive clause is separated by a comma.",
      "If the subject changes, **damit** with a full clause is usually used: **Er fährt mit dem Zug, damit seine Frau mit dem Auto fahren kann**. **Damit** can also appear with the same subject."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "damit: so that, or with that",
     "texto": [
      "As a conjunction, **damit** means \"so that\" and introduces a subordinate clause with the verb at the end: **Ich lerne, damit ich die Prüfung bestehe** (I study so that I pass the exam). It can also be a pronominal adverb meaning \"with that / with it\": **Damit bin ich einverstanden** (I agree with that). The function and verb order allow you to tell both uses apart."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
